Extension API: the Leaders screen's view state on the wire ("OFFS").

STATUS: NOT APPLIED. Written by work order 167, 24 September 2026, and
parked for Data's go/no-go (doc/briefs/167-parked-for-data.md, item W).
orion2re's tree was not touched. What was shown, and only this: the
patch applies to src/ext/ext_api.cpp at orion2re e6199966
(`patch -p1 --dry-run`), and the patched file compiles with the
engine's own flags from out/build/Linux/linux-debug/build.ninja
(g++ -std=gnu++20 -fsyntax-only, the cmake_pch.hxx include, the
ORION2RE_EXT define) — with a control: the same file with one member
name misspelt is refused. It has not run.

To apply, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_officer_screen_state.patch

then rebuild, and add the OFFS marker to tools/version_check.py in the
same commit that records the apply (the pattern of open fixes 27/28).
It comes back off with `patch -R -p1` and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    OFFICER::Officers_Screen_ (officer.cpp:856-1195) keeps everything
    that decides what it shows and what a click does in OFFICER, MOX
    and MAINPUPS globals, and SerializeState touches none of them.
    Without this block an HD client knows the screen is up (29), knows
    the field list and has every leader record — and cannot tell
    which button mode is on (hire, pool, dismiss), which leader is
    selected, which star the colony view shows or has chosen, which
    stack the ship view shows, which ships are in its grid or which of
    them is picked, where that grid is scrolled, or which leader the
    hire popup is offering.

    RECONSTRUCTION WAS TRIED FIRST (decision 25 of the OrionLayer
    fundament):

      - the VIEW and the HIRE mode ARE readable from the field list:
        the ship view adds the scroll arrows `-`/`+` at (613, 22) and
        (613, 170), the colony view does not (officer.cpp:2942-2963);
        hire mode replaces HIRE `H` by CANCEL `X` (:2857-2881). HD
        reads both there today and does not need this block for them.
      - the LISTED LEADERS are a pure function of the leader records
        (Build_Captain_Id_List_, :2705-2730) and HD rebuilds them; the
        block carries the engine's list so the rebuild is CHECKED.
      - POOL and DISMISS mode are not: both buttons stay the same
        hidden fields in modes -1, 1 and 2 (:2831-2855) and only the
        drawn frame differs. Nor is the selection, nor the two stars,
        nor the stack (its ships reach the field list as fourteen
        identical rectangles, :2959), nor the popup's leader.

THE BLOCK, appended after FSEL, only while SCREEN_OFFICERS is up:

    "OFFS"
    int8   _officer_scrn_type        0 ship officers, 1 colony leaders
    int8   _officer_button_mode      -1 none, 0 hire, 1 pool, 2 dismiss
    int8   _officer_selected         leader id or -1
    int8   _officer_scanned          leader id under the pointer or -1
    int16  _officer_star_displayed   star the colony view shows
    int16  _officer_star_chosen      star a leader would be assigned to
    int16  _n_fltscrn_officers       0..4
    int16  _officer_id_list[0..3]    the listed leaders, -1 past the end
    int16  _small_ship_stack_ptr     the ship view's stack, -1 for none
    int16  _ship_stack_start[stack]  its head node, -1 for none
    int16  first_visible_row         of the big-icon grid's scroll bar
    int16  _offpop_big_icon_selected the picked big icon or -1
    int16  _scanned_big_ship         the big icon under the pointer
    int16  _scanned_small_ship       the galaxy box icon under it
    int16  _galaxy_map_scanned_star  the galaxy box star under it
    int16  popup leader              MAINPUPS::_g_officer while the hire
                                     popup is up over this screen, else -1
    int16  popup field state         MAINPUPS::_field_state then, else -1
    int16  N                         big icons
    N x (int16 ship_idx, uint8 selected)   in DISPLAY order

One file, src/ext/ext_api.cpp. Nothing above the block moves, so a
client that stops reading after FSEL is unaffected.

--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -314,6 +314,88 @@
             }
         }
     }
+
+    // 4. The Leaders screen's view state: "OFFS", written ONLY while
+    //    SCREEN_OFFICERS is up, and LAST, so nothing above it moves and
+    //    a client that stops after FSEL is unaffected. It can never
+    //    meet FLTS: that one is written only on SCREEN_FLEET. OrionLayer,
+    //    open fix 30.
+    //
+    //    NOTHING IN THIS BLOCK IS REACHABLE ANY OTHER WAY. Every value
+    //    is an OFFICER, MOX or MAINPUPS global the screen keeps for
+    //    itself (officer.cpp:12-29, mox.cpp) and SerializeState never
+    //    touched. The leader records are on the wire already and the
+    //    four listed leaders can be rebuilt from them
+    //    (Build_Captain_Id_List_ is a pure function, officer.cpp:
+    //    2705-2730), so the list is sent for the client to CHECK its
+    //    reconstruction against, not because it could not be had. What
+    //    cannot be had: which view is up, which button mode (hire, pool,
+    //    dismiss), which leader is selected and which is under the
+    //    pointer, which star the colony view shows and which it has
+    //    chosen, and — in the ship view — which stack, which ships in
+    //    which order and which of them is picked, where the list is
+    //    scrolled. And, while the hire popup runs over this screen
+    //    (mainpups.cpp:784-930, reporting 29 all the while), WHICH
+    //    leader it offers and in which state.
+    //
+    //    The big-icon list is written in DISPLAY order, the order
+    //    Build_Fltscrn_Big_Icon_Fields_ left in _fltscrn_big_icon —
+    //    the same array and the same order FLTS sends.
+    if (current_screen == SCREEN_OFFICERS) {
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'O');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'F');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'F');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'S');
+
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)MOX::_officer_scrn_type);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)OFFICER::_officer_button_mode);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)MOX::_officer_selected);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)MOX::_officer_scanned);
+        Write16(buf, OFFICER::_officer_star_displayed);
+        Write16(buf, OFFICER::_officer_star_chosen);
+
+        int16_t n_officers = MOX::_n_fltscrn_officers;
+        if (n_officers < 0) n_officers = 0;
+        if (n_officers > 4) n_officers = 4;
+        Write16(buf, n_officers);
+        for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+            Write16(buf, MOX::_officer_id_list ? MOX::_officer_id_list[i]
+                                               : (int16_t)-1);
+        }
+
+        int16_t stack = MOX::_small_ship_stack_ptr;
+        int16_t head = -1;
+        if (stack >= 0 && stack < MOX::_ship_stack_count) {
+            head = MOX::_ship_stack_start[stack];
+        } else {
+            stack = -1;
+        }
+        Write16(buf, stack);
+        Write16(buf, head);
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_scroll_bar ? MOX::_scroll_bar->first_visible_row
+                                      : (int16_t)0);
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_offpop_big_icon_selected);
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_scanned_big_ship);
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_scanned_small_ship);
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_galaxy_map_scanned_star);
+
+        // The hire popup, only while it is up over THIS screen: the
+        // flag is set by OFFICER::Hire_Officer_Popup_ for exactly the
+        // popup's lifetime (officer.cpp:3391-3400).
+        bool popup = MAINPUPS::_on_officer_screen_flag != 0;
+        Write16(buf, popup ? MAINPUPS::_g_officer : (int16_t)-1);
+        Write16(buf, popup ? MAINPUPS::_field_state : (int16_t)-1);
+
+        int16_t icons = MOX::_n_fltscrn_big_icons;
+        if (icons < 0) icons = 0;
+        if (icons > SHIP_LIST_CAPACITY) icons = SHIP_LIST_CAPACITY;
+        if (!MOX::_fltscrn_big_icon) icons = 0;
+        Write16(buf, icons);
+        for (int16_t i = 0; i < icons; i++) {
+            Write16(buf, MOX::_fltscrn_big_icon[i].ship_idx);
+            Write8(buf, (uint8_t)(MOX::_fltscrn_big_icon[i].selected != 0));
+        }
+    }
 }
 
